{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39837048",
      "title": "Creating a Custom Hook",
      "sourceHash": "8f105fdeef26de9b2a7a0c61a5445fea2317bcc4613e23f328ef1044944547e7",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.75,
          "end": 3.3,
          "en": "So how could we outsource this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.3,
          "end": 5.04,
          "en": "into a custom hook?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.04,
          "end": 7.59,
          "en": "Well, we can create a new folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.59,
          "end": 11.19,
          "en": "for that in a src folder that could be named hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.19,
          "end": 12.93,
          "en": "but this is totally optional.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.93,
          "end": 15.15,
          "en": "You don't have to create that folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.15,
          "end": 17.37,
          "en": "and you can name it whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.37,
          "end": 19.83,
          "en": "So I'm just doing this to have some structure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 19.83,
          "end": 22.68,
          "en": "in this project and in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 22.68,
          "end": 27.373,
          "en": "we could then add a file that could be named useFetch.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.13,
          "end": 31.71,
          "en": "though this name is also up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.71,
          "end": 36.15,
          "en": "and this notation here might also look a bit weird.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.15,
          "end": 37.53,
          "en": "It's also up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.53,
          "end": 41.34,
          "en": "You could also name it use-fetch like this, or just fetch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.34,
          "end": 44.46,
          "en": "But I'm going for useFetch like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.46,
          "end": 46.38,
          "en": "since this will also be the name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.38,
          "end": 49.29,
          "en": "of the hook I'm about to create.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.29,
          "end": 53.103,
          "en": "And I'll explain why it starts with use in just a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.57,
          "end": 57.78,
          "en": "Now, inside of this useFetch.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.78,
          "end": 60.36,
          "en": "we can now create a custom hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.36,
          "end": 64.653,
          "en": "by simply creating a function, a standard function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.67,
          "end": 68.22,
          "en": "But now, and that's important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.22,
          "end": 71.56,
          "en": "it should be a function that starts with use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.53999999999999,
          "end": 74.46000000000001,
          "en": "because that's a convention.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.46000000000001,
          "end": 79.23,
          "en": "And actually also, basically a rule in React projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.23,
          "end": 84.07,
          "en": "that functions that start with use are treated as hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.96000000000001,
          "end": 89.96000000000001,
          "en": "and React projects typically look for functions that start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90.15,
          "end": 95.15,
          "en": "with use and enforce certain rules on such functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 96.09,
          "end": 99.53999999999999,
          "en": "For example, in App.jsx, if I would try",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.53999999999999,
          "end": 103.5,
          "en": "to use the built-in useState hook nested inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 103.5,
          "end": 105.18,
          "en": "of some other code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 105.18,
          "end": 107.763,
          "en": "you would see that here I'm getting an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108.78,
          "end": 110.61,
          "en": "I'm getting red squiggly lines",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 110.61,
          "end": 113.91,
          "en": "and the information that a React hook must be called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.91,
          "end": 117.6,
          "en": "in a React function or a custom hook function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.6,
          "end": 119.83,
          "en": "So basically what I told you before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 121.08,
          "end": 125.16,
          "en": "but technically, this would be valid JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 125.16,
          "end": 127.89,
          "en": "because useState is just a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.89,
          "end": 131.793,
          "en": "and theoretically, you can call functions anywhere.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 132.75,
          "end": 135.03,
          "en": "This is a rule that's instead enforced",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 135.03,
          "end": 138.39,
          "en": "by this project setup, and which can only be enforced",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 138.39,
          "end": 140.56,
          "en": "because of the name of this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 141.42000000000002,
          "end": 142.92000000000002,
          "en": "because this project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 142.92000000000002,
          "end": 145.92000000000002,
          "en": "like most React projects is configured",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 145.92000000000002,
          "end": 149.76,
          "en": "such that functions that start with use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 149.76,
          "end": 151.68,
          "en": "are treated as hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 151.68,
          "end": 155.37,
          "en": "and that those rules of hooks are enforced",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 155.37,
          "end": 158.91,
          "en": "on such functions so that we, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 158.91,
          "end": 162.453,
          "en": "get an error if we try to use them in the wrong place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 164.34,
          "end": 168.42000000000002,
          "en": "That's why your custom hook function also must start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 168.42000000000002,
          "end": 172.23,
          "en": "with use so that those rules are also enforced",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 172.23,
          "end": 174.18,
          "en": "on this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 174.18,
          "end": 178.05,
          "en": "And these rules are important because without them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 178.05,
          "end": 180.36,
          "en": "if using hooks in the wrong place,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 180.36,
          "end": 184.053,
          "en": "your applications could break or behave incorrectly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 185.31,
          "end": 187.83,
          "en": "But of course, use is just a part of the name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 187.83,
          "end": 191.01,
          "en": "Here I wanna name my hook useFetch,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 191.01,
          "end": 193.47,
          "en": "though the name is, of course, up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 193.47,
          "end": 196.14,
          "en": "You just should make sure that you don't clash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 196.14,
          "end": 200.163,
          "en": "with built-in hook names like useState or useEffect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 201.78,
          "end": 204.93,
          "en": "But now this is recognized as a hook function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 204.93,
          "end": 208.803,
          "en": "and you can now use other hooks inside of this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 209.67000000000002,
          "end": 212.01,
          "en": "This allows you to, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 212.01,
          "end": 214.263,
          "en": "outsource this useEffect code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 215.25,
          "end": 220.25,
          "en": "We can copy that and paste that into the useFetch function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 220.86,
          "end": 224.91,
          "en": "And now import useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 224.91,
          "end": 228.993,
          "en": "from react and React won't complain.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 229.95,
          "end": 232.23,
          "en": "It will complain about some other things here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 232.23,
          "end": 236.103,
          "en": "which we have to fix but using useEffect here is fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 236.97,
          "end": 240.39,
          "en": "If I would name this function just fetch without use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 240.39,
          "end": 243.63,
          "en": "you would see I'm getting some red squiggly lines here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 243.63,
          "end": 246.63,
          "en": "and I'm getting an error that this must only be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 246.63,
          "end": 250.113,
          "en": "in a React component function or a custom hook function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 250.98,
          "end": 254.67,
          "en": "But with use in front of that name, everything is fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 254.67,
          "end": 259.56,
          "en": "But why would we put this code into our custom hook?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 259.56,
          "end": 262.23,
          "en": "And how should this custom hook work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 262.23,
          "end": 264.153,
          "en": "What's the idea behind it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 265.41,
          "end": 268.95,
          "en": "Well, the idea is that in the end later,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 268.95,
          "end": 273.81,
          "en": "we'll be able to get rid of useEffect here in App.jsx",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 273.81,
          "end": 277.65,
          "en": "and that instead, we can simply use our custom hook here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 277.65,
          "end": 281.64,
          "en": "and that will then internally perform all the work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 281.64,
          "end": 283.5,
          "en": "we stored in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 283.5,
          "end": 287.25,
          "en": "But our component function therefore got leaner.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 287.25,
          "end": 289.23,
          "en": "And we could use that same hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 289.23,
          "end": 293.61,
          "en": "in other components that would then perform the same work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 293.61,
          "end": 297.9,
          "en": "And that's, of course, in general in programming, the idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 297.9,
          "end": 302.07,
          "en": "behind creating functions that you can create them once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 302.07,
          "end": 304.11,
          "en": "and that you can then use them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 304.11,
          "end": 308.58,
          "en": "in different places of your application to trigger them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 308.58,
          "end": 310.56,
          "en": "And here we wanna do the same",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 310.56,
          "end": 313.44,
          "en": "with the special condition that we want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 313.44,
          "end": 316.38,
          "en": "to use built-in hooks like useEffect in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 316.38,
          "end": 318.93,
          "en": "and that's why we have to build a custom hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 318.93,
          "end": 322.56,
          "en": "which we simply do by adding use in front of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 322.56,
          "end": 325.8,
          "en": "But of course, this hook is not done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 325.8,
          "end": 328.2,
          "en": "What else do we have to do in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 328.2,
          "end": 330.243,
          "en": "to make this hook functional?",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}